# The native shell's local environment — the committed TEMPLATE. Copy it to
# `native/.env` (gitignored, and kept out of the EAS upload by .easignore) and
# fill in what you need; every value is optional for a local build.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS READ BY THE EAS CLI FROM THIS FILE — it reads the PROCESS
# environment. Export the values (or set them as CI secrets/variables) before
# `eas build`; a shell that merely has a `.env` beside it has exported nothing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EAS. Only needed to drive builds non-interactively (CI does this with the
# EXPO_TOKEN repo secret); a laptop uses `eas login` instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# An Expo access token. Authenticates the EAS CLI with no interactive login,
# and takes precedence over any `eas login` session on the same machine.
#
# WHERE: https://expo.dev/settings/access-tokens → **Create token** → copy it
# (shown once). A ROBOT token (https://expo.dev/accounts/<account>/settings/
# access-tokens) is the right kind for CI: it cannot sign in to the dashboard
# and owns no projects, so its blast radius is bounded. The GitHub workflow
# that drives EAS (.github/workflows/native.yml, manual dispatch only) reads it
# from the `EXPO_TOKEN` repo secret, so on CI it is set there rather than here.
# SHAPE: an opaque string, no fixed prefix. Treat it as a password.
# EXPO_TOKEN=

# The Expo project this app builds under, until it is pinned in app.config.js.
#
# WHERE: `eas init` creates the project and prints its id (also on the project
# page at https://expo.dev/accounts/<account>/projects/<slug>). Once the
# project exists, pin the id in app.config.js (`EAS_PROJECT_ID`) so nobody
# needs this variable; CI reads it from the `EAS_PROJECT_ID` repo variable
# until then.
# SHAPE: a lowercase UUID, 8-4-4-4-12.
# EAS_PROJECT_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-time escape hatch. For LOCAL builds only — a store build must not set
# it. Left commented out on purpose. See docs/configuration.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Points the WebView at a deployed slot instead of the copy of the game bundled
# inside the app. Debugging only: a store build that streams the website is the
# exact shape App Store guideline 4.2 rejects.
# VALUE: any URL the device can reach — a deploy slot on the live origin, or
# your dev server on the LAN (http://<your-lan-ip>:5173/, not localhost, which
# on a phone means the phone).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GAME_URL=https://game2.niclaslindstedt.se/preview/
